Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• event_date : filter for the month 202012 (December‑2020).  
• event_name : keep only the “purchase” events.  
• items      : repeated record that contains the line‑items of every purchase; fields used  
  – item_name  : to find “Google Navy Speckled Tee” and every other product name.  
  – quantity   : to sum how many units of every product were bought.  
  – transaction_id (inside the ecommerce struct, or the same value repeated in every
   item record) : to recognise which line‑items belong to the same order so we can
   check “what was bought together”.  
• ecommerce.transaction_id : the order / receipt id that ties the items of the same
  purchase together.  
• user_pseudo_id : optional, to see which customers purchased the Tee.  

Typical conditions  

WHERE event_name = 'purchase'  
  AND event_date BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'  
  AND LOWER(item.item_name) LIKE '%google%navy%speckled%tee%'  

